  "description": "A standalone event-expectation node for FluxFlow: post ProjectionEvent values, watch for a matching event (expect) or its absence (guard), and broadcast one EventExpectationResult with error/event ports. No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Expectations",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T14:31:34.997Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "NvND0p67rP3yucr3PehKr8bCQS8FYZC0mo0mh3FaqgghbvKN9MjRTHgQSa68/BgrivSdV0Q1uK4KakJmMxhRmQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 39128,
  "published": "2026-06-19T14:28:05.08Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt as a single standalone event-expectation node over the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: post FlowMessage<ProjectionEvent> in, one FlowMessage<EventExpectationResult> broadcast out, failures on the error port, diagnostics on the event port. The node resolves on the first of a matching event, a timeout armed over the injected TimeProvider, or input completion via CompleteWithResultAsync. The engine glue (node factory, module, registration extensions, component-type/port constants, JSON options reader, component-options/clock holder, and design-metadata provider) is removed; the node depends only on FluxFlow.Nodes and the shared FluxFlow.Components.Projections contracts (ProjectionEvent, EventFilter), and runs without the engine. ProjectionEvent replaces the engine FlowEvent as the standalone input contract; correlation flows event -> result via the envelope.",
